# Web design quality (Dockyrd dashboard)

Fits **`frontend-evaluator`** + [dockyard-design-contract](../dockyard-design-contract.mdc).

## Before implementing UI

1. Read **`docs/design-index.json`** for the route (nav, tokens, shared blocks).
2. Open the matching artboard in **`docs/dockyrd-design.html`** (or issue wireframe for §17 gaps).
3. Reuse **`web/components/dockyard/ui/*`** (primitives) and composites under **`web/components/dockyard/*`** before one-off page markup. Storybook stories must import those same modules — [storybook-ui-source](../storybook-ui-source.mdc).
4. Align with `docs/project/project.md` and issue spec when on Feature track.

Do **not** wait for design approval. Do **not** freestyle IA that contradicts the design index (e.g. re-add removed header actions).

## Anti-template

Avoid generic SaaS placeholders that ignore the Calendly-inspired spec: wrong grays, default shadcn demo skin, unmotivated centered heroes on **app** pages (marketing site is out of scope for MVP panel).

Push for: hierarchy, spacing rhythm, semantic status pills, intentional hover/focus, Geist + Geist Mono roles from tokens.

## Shadows

**Default: no decorative drop shadows** on cards, rows, inputs, sidebar. Prefer surface + border (`#ECEAE6`). Allow shadows only for floating overlays (dialogs, popovers, command palette).

## Component checklist

- [ ] Matches design-index structure for the route (sidebar, header, tabs, primary CTA)
- [ ] Status pills / stat tiles / resource rows use shared dockyard components
- [ ] Empty / loading / error states when AC requires them
- [ ] `aria-current`, `aria-label` on icon controls; touch targets ≥ 44px where specified
- [ ] English UI copy; product name **Dockyrd** in chrome
